{"name":"Abyssal Depths","hex":"#10246a","fetched":"2026-10-19","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"abyssal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Belonging to, or resembling, an abyss; unfathomable. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Of or belonging to the ocean depths, especially below 2000 metres (6500 ft): abyssal zone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/abyssal"},{"term":"depths","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of depth"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The deepest part. (Usually of a body of water.)","A very remote part."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/depths"}],"entries":[{"title":"Abyssal zone","blocks":[{"text":"The abyssal zone or abyssopelagic zone is a layer of the pelagic zone of the ocean. The word abyss comes from the Greek word ἄβυσσος, meaning \"bottomless\". At depths of 4,000–6,000 m (13,000–20,000 ft), this zone remains in perpetual darkness. It extends across 83% of the total area of the ocean and 60% of Earth's surface. The abyssal zone has temperatures around 2–3 °C (36–37 °F) through the large majority of its mass. The water pressure can reach up to 76 MPa."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abyssal_zone","wikidata":"Q242857"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Beebe_ShrimpChimney_Close.jpg/500px-Beebe_ShrimpChimney_Close.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Beebe_ShrimpChimney_Close.jpg/1280px-Beebe_ShrimpChimney_Close.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Beebe_ShrimpChimney_Close.jpg/500px-Beebe_ShrimpChimney_Close.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A dense gathering of Rimicaris hybisae shrimp at the Beebe Hydrothermal Vent Field in the Mid-Cayman Rise. The shrimp are almost entirely blind, surviving at the interface of cold, deep seawater and supercritical hydrothermal fluid.[13]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeebe_ShrimpChimney_Close.jpg"}],"sounds":{"abyssal":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/41/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-abyssal.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/41/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-abyssal.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-abyssal.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/41/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-abyssal.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Persent101-abyssal.wav.ogg"}],"depths":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/21/En-us-depths.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/21/En-us-depths.ogg/En-us-depths.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Innenhafen Duisburg Blaue Stunde 2014","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Innenhafen_Duisburg_Blaue_Stunde_2014.jpg/500px-Innenhafen_Duisburg_Blaue_Stunde_2014.jpg","ratio":1.6818845872899928,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Innenhafen_Duisburg_Blaue_Stunde_2014.jpg","share":0.106875},{"title":"ADAC-Zentrale, Munich, March 2017-05","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/ADAC-Zentrale%2C_Munich%2C_March_2017-05.jpg/500px-ADAC-Zentrale%2C_Munich%2C_March_2017-05.jpg","ratio":1.4909165978530141,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ADAC-Zentrale,_Munich,_March_2017-05.jpg","share":0.0725},{"title":"2018 01 (Blue) - Chaouen","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/2018_01_%28Blue%29_-_Chaouen.jpg/500px-2018_01_%28Blue%29_-_Chaouen.jpg","ratio":1.